WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:04.900
The cliffhanger is one of the most important
weapons writers can have in their arsenals.

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:09.360
When done right, cliffhangers leave the audience
breathless, dying to see what happens next.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.210
Then again, there are some endings that just
dangle off that cliff forever.

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:17.030
Here are some famous cliffhangers that will
never have a resolution.

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:18.830
Spider-Man: The Animated Series

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:23.289
Back in the '90s. one of the few bright spots
for the then-struggling Marvel Comics company

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:28.279
was Spider-Man: The Animated Series, which
ended on a humdinger of a cliffhanger.

00:00:28.279 --> 00:00:34.030
Peter discovered his new bride, Mary Jane,
was actually a clone, after the real MJ was

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:37.030
knocked through an inter-dimensional portal
by Green Goblin.

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:41.141
The plan was for Spidey to rescue her at the
beginning of the sixth season, but after a

00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:45.950
dispute between execs at Marvel and Fox, the
network abruptly ended the series.

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:49.670
"Wait Peter, there's so much I have to ask
you!"

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:53.710
The show's head writer later apologized to
traumatized fans who are still wondering if

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:57.960
Mary Jane ended up just stuck in another dimension
forever.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:58.960
Planet of The Apes

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:02.190
"Eh.. the movie or the planet?"

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:07.450
At the end of Tim Burton's poorly received
2001 version of The Planet of the Apes, Mark

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:12.399
Wahlberg travels through time, pursued by
his evil ape nemesis Thade.

00:01:12.399 --> 00:01:17.850
Wahlberg seemingly wins, but when he returns
to present-day Washington D.C., he discovers

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:23.060
that the Lincoln Memorial is now dedicated
to Thade — instead of Abe.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:24.619
So how did this happen?

00:01:24.619 --> 00:01:27.319
And what does it mean for Wahlberg and humanity?

00:01:27.319 --> 00:01:31.689
Those are questions that will never be answered,
as Burton has said he'd rather jump out a

00:01:31.689 --> 00:01:33.880
window than make a sequel.

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:34.920
"What?

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:35.959
no."

00:01:35.959 --> 00:01:37.149
My Name Is Earl

00:01:37.149 --> 00:01:41.810
For four seasons, Jason Lee's do-gooding lottery
winner went around checking things off his

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:43.770
karma building to-do list.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:49.169
But there's one thing My Name Is Earl didn't
check off: the resolution to the series cliffhanger,

00:01:49.169 --> 00:01:52.569
which promised to reveal the real parentage
of Earl, Jr.

00:01:52.569 --> 00:01:57.000
Fans were especially irate that NBC canceled
the series considering the finale ended with

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.849
a "To Be Continued" graphic.

00:01:58.849 --> 00:02:04.100
There were some discussions between show creator
Greg Garcia and TBS about continuing the series

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:07.149
to provide closure to fans, but costs proved
too high.

00:02:07.149 --> 00:02:08.149
The Event

00:02:08.149 --> 00:02:13.540
NBC heavily promoted The Event, built around
the idea of an impending incident that would

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:15.599
change humanity forever.

00:02:15.599 --> 00:02:20.409
At the end of the first season, viewers learned
that "the event" was aliens creating a massive

00:02:20.409 --> 00:02:24.120
vortex that brings their entire planet into
orbit next to Earth.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:29.280
Oh, and the President's wife reveals she's
secretly one of the aliens, so Mr. President

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:30.769
has an alien baby mama.

00:02:30.769 --> 00:02:32.439
Who wrote this, Jerry Springer?

00:02:32.439 --> 00:02:37.000
Unfortunately for fans, ratings dropped like
a rock after the overhyped premiere, and the

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:38.390
series was canceled.

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:42.430
Series creator Nick Wauters promised that
"one way or another," they would continue

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:43.430
the story.

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:44.960
But so far, that hasn't happened.

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:46.079
Talk about a non-event.

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:49.180
V: The Series

00:02:49.189 --> 00:02:55.069
When the alien invasion opus V debuted on
NBC as a mini-series in May 1983, it captured

00:02:55.069 --> 00:02:59.879
the imagination of the United States, with
an astounding 40 percent of the country tuning

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:00.879
in.

00:03:00.879 --> 00:03:04.280
But while creator Kenneth Johnson pushed for
the story to continue with a series of two-hour

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:09.379
movies, NBC wanted a sequel mini-series, followed
by a new, weekly series.

00:03:09.379 --> 00:03:12.549
So Johnson did what any creative type might:
he quit.

00:03:12.549 --> 00:03:17.530
NBC went forward without him, but the resulting
series was somehow both expensive to make

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:18.880
and also pretty poorly done.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:19.580
"Now!"

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:32.980
The final episode had multiple cliffhangers,
with human-Visitor hybrid "Starchild" Elizabeth

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:38.040
Maxwell agreeing to return with their leader
to the Visitors' planet, her boyfriend stowing

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:41.420
away on their shuttle, and Diana planting
a bomb on the ship.

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:44.129
And then, well, nothing.

00:03:44.129 --> 00:03:45.859
Because NBC canceled the series.

00:03:45.859 --> 00:03:49.920
But it wouldn't be the last time fans of V
would be left hanging…

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:55.530
ABC revived V as a brand-new series in 2009,
and in doing so, the network ignored all that

00:03:55.530 --> 00:04:01.140
came before — except for having ladies eating
rodents and totally messing with fans by going

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:03.950
out on an unresolved cliffhanger.

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:09.689
This time around, the lizard queen completely
conquered Earth, with the last fugitive humans

00:04:09.689 --> 00:04:12.400
literally going underground to lead a resistance
movement.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:16.799
And as far as we know, they're still down
there somewhere, huddling in the dark, waiting

00:04:16.799 --> 00:04:19.590
for a third season that will never arrive.

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:22.210
Poor, sad fools.

00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:23.210
Survivors

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:28.530
The feelgood BBC drama Survivors featured
the joyous premise of Earth's population being

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:32.670
almost totally wiped out by a super-flu released
by an evil corporation.

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:34.570
"How many millions.

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:39.550
If the infection carries on progressing at
the current rate, you're talking more than

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:41.060
90% of the world's population."

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:45.610
At the end of the second season, Tom, a former
convict who found his redemption over the

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:51.800
course of the series, stows away on the corporation's
plane — angry, armed and waiting in hiding

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.500
to exact revenge.

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:58.150
It was the BBC, though, that got its revenge
on the show for giving them poor ratings by

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:00.280
never airing a third season.

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:01.900
That's… sick.

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:03.030
The River

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:08.860
When famous explorer Emmet Cole disappears
while seeking the secret of magic in the Amazon,

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:14.760
his family decides to take a cruise up the
Amazon River and find him in ABC's 2012 found-footage

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:20.110
series The River, which had none other than
Steven Spielberg and Paranormal Activity creator

00:05:20.110 --> 00:05:21.650
Oren Peli attached.

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:26.000
And those famous names meant exactly squat
when it came to ratings,

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:28.540
"Oh my god!

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:29.720
Get him down!"

00:05:29.729 --> 00:05:33.400
which is too bad for fans, because the series
ended with a shock twist.

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:39.009
The mystical spirit of the Amazon itself actually
warped reality to strand everyone in the middle

00:05:39.009 --> 00:05:42.419
of the jungle just as they seemed to have
made their escape.

00:05:42.419 --> 00:05:46.539
Netflix considered picking the show up for
a second season, but wisely opted against

00:05:46.539 --> 00:05:47.539
it.

00:05:47.539 --> 00:05:50.520
Because why mess with angry gods if you don't
have to?

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:51.720
The Italian Job

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:56.990
The original 1969 version of The Italian Job
featured superstar Michael Caine teaming up

00:05:56.990 --> 00:05:59.680
with a bunch of crooks to steal $4 million
in gold.

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:04.009
They get away with the loot, but in a last
second twist, their escape vehicle goes off

00:06:04.009 --> 00:06:06.280
a cliff with all the gold inside.

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:11.340
Not to worry, though, because Caine has a
plan to deal with this literal cliffhanger.

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:14.360
"Hang on a minute lads.

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:16.419
I've got a great idea."

00:06:16.419 --> 00:06:19.930
Just what that great idea was, though, nobody
ever found out.

00:06:19.930 --> 00:06:25.250
Like that bus almost certainly did, the film
itself also crashed and burned, and the planned

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:26.900
sequel was never made.

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:28.030
Thanks for watching!

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:30.569
Click the Grunge icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:30.569 --> 00:06:32.809
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

